<title>HUNGARY: Hungary cuts 3-mth rediscount bill to 21.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary cuts 3-mth rediscount bill to 21.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Monday it will cut its three-month bill rediscount rate to an annual 21.75 percent from the current 23.10 percent, effective November 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The rediscount rate was modified to bring it in line with the bank's base rate,&quot; the NBH said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
